    "captions": [
      { "t": 0.0, "text": "About 86,000 Romans and allies face Hannibal's 50,000. The Romans stack their infantry unusually deep, hoping sheer weight will punch through." },
      { "t": 0.5, "text": "By the river, Hasdrubal's heavy Spanish and Gallic horse crash into the Roman cavalry. There is no room to manoeuvre; men dismount and fight on foot." },
      { "t": 1.2, "text": "The Roman cavalry is cut down or flees. Consul Paullus, wounded, joins the infantry. On the far wing, Numidian light horse keep the allied cavalry busy." },
      { "t": 1.9, "text": "Hannibal's centre bulges toward the Romans: a crescent of Gauls and Spaniards, with Hannibal himself behind it. The Roman infantry hits it head on." },
      { "t": 2.4, "text": "Hasdrubal does not chase the beaten horsemen. He leads his cavalry right round the back of the Roman army." },
      { "t": 2.9, "text": "The crescent gives ground slowly, as planned, and turns inside out. The Romans pour into the pocket, packed tighter and tighter." },
      { "t": 3.4, "text": "Hasdrubal hits the allied cavalry from behind. It breaks, and the Numidians chase it off the field." },
      { "t": 3.7, "text": "Now the African infantry, waiting unseen on each flank, turn inward and attack the Roman sides." },
      { "t": 4.5, "text": "Hasdrubal turns back and charges into the rear of the Roman infantry. The trap is closed." },
      { "t": 5.2, "text": "Surrounded and crushed together, the Roman army is destroyed. Livy says 48,200 died, Polybius 70,000. Hannibal lost perhaps 6,000 to 8,000." }
    ]
  },

