    "captions": [
      { "t": 0.0, "text": "Late spring 218 BC. Hannibal leaves New Carthage with, Polybius says, about 90,000 infantry, 12,000 cavalry and 37 elephants." },
      { "t": 1.1, "text": "North of the Ebro he fights his way through the local tribes and leaves garrisons behind him." },
      { "t": 2.5, "text": "Over the Pyrenees and into Gaul. Consul Publius Scipio, meant to stop him in Spain, sails west from Pisa." },
      { "t": 3.3, "text": "At the Rhône, Gauls hold the far bank. Hannibal sends a force upstream to hit them from behind, and floats the elephants across on rafts." },
      { "t": 3.6, "text": "Scipio lands at Massalia and reaches the crossing three days too late. He sends his army on to Spain and hurries back to Italy." },
      { "t": 4.4, "text": "Up into the Alps as winter closes in. Mountain tribes ambush the column in the passes." },
      { "t": 5.1, "text": "At the top, Hannibal shows his exhausted men the plains of Italy below. The descent is worse: snow, ice and a landslide that has to be cut through." },
      { "t": 5.7, "text": "He reaches the Po valley with about 20,000 infantry and 6,000 cavalry. The crossing took fifteen days." },
      { "t": 6.5, "text": "First clash, a cavalry fight at the Ticinus. Scipio is wounded; legend says his teenage son, the future Africanus, saved him." },
      { "t": 7.4, "text": "December: Hannibal wins at the Trebia, and the Gauls of northern Italy flock to join him." }
    ]
  }
